./LOGBOOK.md:83:- BLOCKER: `.spec/security-privacy.md` requires private keys and passphrases to live in the Data Protection Keychain "shared only through the minimum keychain access group required by the app and its packet tunnel extension" (also `.spec/threat-model.md` DF-02/M-02). On macOS that is unsatisfiable. Developer ID direct distribution forces the provider to be a **system extension** (TN3134, `.spec/platform-distribution.md`), a sysex runs **as root** outside a user context, the Data Protection Keychain is available only to code in a user context, and keychain access groups share items between programs running as the **same** user. The host runs as the logged-in user. iOS is unaffected — its appex runs as the same user as its host.
